# youtube.dadl — YouTube Data API v3 for ToolMesh
# Read video metadata, status and statistics, and update a video's visibility and
# snippet (title, description, tags) without losing fields the caller did not touch.
#
# Domain Notes for LLM consumers:
# - SCOPE: this file is deliberately narrow. It covers what a release workflow needs:
#   read videos by ID, switch a video between private / unlisted / public, and edit its
#   snippet. No upload, no search, no comments, no playlists (see coverage.missing).
# - AUTH is OAuth 2.0 with a user-delegated refresh token. There is no service-account
#   path for YouTube channels and an API key can only read public data. The token is
#   bound to ONE channel: the channel (personal or brand account) picked on the Google
#   account chooser during the one-time consent. Call list_channels to see which channel
#   the stored token belongs to. Videos of other channels can be read while they are
#   public or unlisted, but never updated.
# - VISIBILITY: status.privacyStatus is one of "private", "unlisted", "public". An
#   unlisted video is reachable by link and embeddable but does not show up in search,
#   feeds or the channel page. A scheduled video (status.publishAt set) MUST be private
#   until the scheduled time; unlisted and scheduled cannot be combined.
# - videos.update REPLACES whole parts. For every part named in the `part` parameter,
#   each mutable property that is missing from the request body is reset or deleted:
#   updating only snippet.description without sending snippet.tags deletes the tags.
#   snippet.title and snippet.categoryId are REQUIRED whenever part contains snippet.
#   Therefore never call the raw update directly. The update_video composite reads the
#   video first, merges the requested changes into the current values and sends the
#   complete parts back. Unchanged input means no write at all.
# - READ-AFTER-WRITE: videos.list can still return the PREVIOUS privacyStatus for a few
#   seconds after a successful videos.update (observed: still the old value 1.6 s after
#   the PUT, correct shortly afterwards). The update response itself is authoritative.
#   A verification read right after an update must retry with backoff (10 to 30 s)
#   before it reports a failure. Thumbnail URLs changing form is not a field change:
#   private videos get signed i9.ytimg.com URLs, unlisted and public videos plain
#   i.ytimg.com URLs.
# - Mutable snippet properties: title, description, tags[], categoryId, defaultLanguage,
#   defaultAudioLanguage. Mutable status properties: privacyStatus, embeddable, license,
#   publicStatsViewable, publishAt, selfDeclaredMadeForKids, containsSyntheticMedia.
#   Everything else (publishedAt, channelId, thumbnails, uploadStatus, madeForKids, ...)
#   is read-only.
# - status.containsSyntheticMedia is the creator's disclosure that the video contains
#   realistic altered or synthetic (AI-generated) content. The merge keeps it as it is
#   unless the caller sets it.
# - DESCRIPTION EDITS: the description is one plain-text field, max 5000 bytes, no
#   angle brackets. To swap a single line (for example a link that changes when a page
#   goes live) use replace_line_prefix + replace_line_with on update_video: exactly one
#   line must start with the prefix; if none does but a line already equals the
#   replacement, nothing changes. This makes the call safe to repeat.
# - QUOTA: every request costs units from a per-project daily budget (default 10,000,
#   reset at midnight Pacific Time). videos.list = 1 unit per call (regardless of the
#   number of IDs or parts), channels.list = 1 unit, videos.update = 50 units. One
#   update_video call that changes something costs 51 units (1 read + 1 write), an
#   unchanged one 1 unit. Exceeding the budget returns 403 with reason quotaExceeded.
# - IDs: a video ID is the 11-character value from the watch URL
#   (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID). list_videos accepts up to 50 IDs,
#   comma-separated. Unknown IDs and private videos of other channels are silently
#   absent from the result (empty array, not 404).
# - `part` controls which sections of a resource are returned. Useful values for
#   videos: snippet, status, statistics, contentDetails. Numbers in statistics arrive
#   as strings ("viewCount": "42").
# - Error envelope: { "error": { "code": 403, "message": "...", "errors": [ { "domain":
#   "youtube.quota", "reason": "quotaExceeded", "message": "..." } ] } }. The reason
#   (quotaExceeded, forbidden, videoNotFound, invalidVideoMetadata, invalidCategoryId,
#   defaultLanguageNotSet, ...) is the stable machine-readable part.
# - Refresh-token lifetime: an OAuth app whose consent screen is in "Testing" status
#   gets refresh tokens that EXPIRE AFTER 7 DAYS. Publish the app to "In production"
#   before the consent. A production token stays valid until the user revokes access,
#   it stays unused for six months, or more than 100 tokens exist for the same client
#   and account. A revoked token shows up as "invalid_grant" on the next call.
spec: "https://dadl.ai/spec/dadl-spec-v0.2.md"
credits:
  - "Dunkel Cloud GmbH -- maintainer"
source_name: "YouTube Data API v3"
source_url: https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/docs
date: "2026-10-19"

backend:
  name: youtube
  type: rest
  version: "1.0"
  base_url: https://www.googleapis.com
  description: >
    YouTube Data API v3 — read videos (metadata, visibility, statistics) by ID and
    update a video's visibility, title, description and tags with a read-merge-write
    that keeps every field the caller did not change.

  coverage:
    endpoints: 3
    total_endpoints: 52
    percentage: 6
    focus: "Video release workflow: videos, visibility, description, channel."
    missing: >
      Everything outside reading and updating existing videos: video upload, delete and
      rating, thumbnails, captions, playlists and playlist items, search, comments and
      comment threads, subscriptions, channel sections and branding, members, activities,
      i18n and category lookups, live streaming (separate API).
    last_reviewed: "2026-10-19"

  setup:
    credential_steps:
      - "Open https://console.cloud.google.com and create or select a Google Cloud project."
      - "Enable the API: APIs & Services → Library → 'YouTube Data API v3' → Enable. No billing account is needed; the default quota is 10,000 units per day."
      - "Configure the OAuth consent screen (Google Auth Platform → Branding / Audience): user type 'External', add an app name and contact address. Then set the publishing status to 'In production'. CRITICAL: an app left in 'Testing' issues refresh tokens that expire after 7 days. The scope used here is a sensitive scope; an unverified production app shows a warning page during consent ('Google hasn't verified this app' → Advanced → continue), which is fine for your own account."
      - "Create the client: Google Auth Platform → Clients → Create client → application type 'Web application', authorized redirect URI https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground. Download the client JSON right away: it holds client_id and client_secret together, and the console shows the secret in full only once. Copy the client ID in full from the client's detail page; it ends with .apps.googleusercontent.com. An ID and a secret from different clients fail later with invalid_client ('The provided client secret is invalid')."
      - "One-time consent: open https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground, open the settings (gear icon), tick 'Use your own OAuth credentials' and enter the client ID and secret; keep 'Access type: Offline' and tick 'Force prompt: Consent Screen'. In step 1 enter the scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.force-ssl and click 'Authorize APIs'."
      - "On the Google account chooser pick the CHANNEL you want to manage. If the channel is a brand account it appears as its own entry below your personal account. The token is bound to exactly this channel."
      - "In step 2 click 'Exchange authorization code for tokens' and copy the refresh token."
      - "Store the three values as ToolMesh credentials: CREDENTIAL_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID, CREDENTIAL_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET, CREDENTIAL_YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN. Then recreate the ToolMesh container (docker compose up -d toolmesh): a plain docker compose restart keeps the old environment and therefore the old values."
      - "Verify: call list_channels. It must return the channel you picked. Then call list_videos with the ID of one of its videos; a private or unlisted video of that channel must be visible."
      - "If calls later fail with 'invalid_grant', the refresh token was revoked or expired: repeat the consent step and replace CREDENTIAL_YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN."
    env_var: CREDENTIAL_YOUTUBE_REFRESH_TOKEN
    backends_yaml: |
      - name: youtube
        transport: rest
        dadl: youtube.dadl
        url: "https://www.googleapis.com"
    required_scopes:
      - "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.force-ssl"
    optional_scopes:
      - "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly"
    docs_url: "https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/guides/auth/server-side-web-apps"
    notes: >
      YouTube has no service-account access to channels; the refresh_token flow with a
      one-time interactive consent is the only headless option. ToolMesh exchanges the
      refresh token for short-lived access tokens on demand, no external refresh job is
      needed. The scope youtube.force-ssl allows reading and editing the channel's
      videos; youtube.readonly is enough if only list_videos and list_channels are used.
      The consent binds the token to one channel, so one backend instance manages one
      channel. Quota is counted per Google Cloud project: 1 unit per read, 50 units per
      video update, 10,000 units per day by default.

  auth:
    type: oauth2
    flow: refresh_token
    token_url: https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token
    client_id_credential: youtube_client_id
    client_secret_credential: youtube_client_secret
    refresh_token_credential: youtube_refresh_token
    refresh_before_expiry: 60s
    # Consent-time scope, documentational only: scopes are not sent on the
    # refresh_token grant, they are fixed when the user consents.
    scopes:
      - "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.force-ssl"

  defaults:
    headers:
      Accept: application/json
    # No pagination block: the covered calls address resources by ID or by owner and
    # return everything in one response.
    errors:
      format: json
      message_path: "$.error.message"
      code_path: "$.error.errors[0].reason"
      retry_on: [500, 502, 503, 504]
      terminal: [400, 401, 403, 404, 409]
      retry_strategy:
        max_retries: 2
        backoff: exponential
        initial_delay: 1s
    response:
      result_path: "$.items"

  tools:

    # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Videos
    # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_videos:
      method: GET
      path: /youtube/v3/videos
      access: read
      description: >
        Read one or more videos by ID. Returns an array of video resources with the
        requested parts: snippet (title, description, tags, categoryId, channelId,
        publishedAt, defaultLanguage), status (privacyStatus = private | unlisted |
        public, publishAt, embeddable, license, madeForKids, containsSyntheticMedia),
        statistics (viewCount, likeCount, commentCount, all as strings). Unknown IDs and
        private videos of other channels are missing from the array (no 404); an empty
        array means "not found or not visible to the authorized channel". In the first
        seconds after a videos.update the result can still show the previous
        privacyStatus; when verifying an update, retry with backoff instead of trusting
        one immediate read. Costs 1 quota unit per call regardless of the number of IDs.
      params:
        id:
          type: string
          in: query
          required: true
          description: "Video ID, or up to 50 IDs separated by commas. The ID is the 11-character v= value of the watch URL."
        part:
          type: string
          in: query
          default: "snippet,status,statistics"
          description: "Comma-separated resource parts to return: snippet, status, statistics, contentDetails, localizations, topicDetails, player."
      pagination: none

    _update_video_raw:
      method: PUT
      path: /youtube/v3/videos
      access: write
      description: >
        Internal: raw videos.update. REPLACES every part named in `part`; mutable
        properties missing from the body are deleted, and snippet requires title and
        categoryId. Use the update_video composite instead, which reads the video and
        merges. Costs 50 quota units.
      params:
        part:
          type: string
          in: query
          required: true
          description: "Parts the body contains and the API should overwrite, for example snippet,status."
        id:
          type: string
          in: body
          required: true
          description: "ID of the video to update. Must belong to the authorized channel."
        snippet:
          type: object
          in: body
          description: "Complete snippet: title, description, categoryId, tags, defaultLanguage, defaultAudioLanguage."
        status:
          type: object
          in: body
          description: "Complete status: privacyStatus, embeddable, license, publicStatsViewable, publishAt, selfDeclaredMadeForKids, containsSyntheticMedia."
      response:
        result_path: "$"
      pagination: none

    # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    # Channels
    # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    list_channels:
      method: GET
      path: /youtube/v3/channels
      access: read
      description: >
        List the channel the stored OAuth token belongs to (mine=true). Returns an array,
        normally with one channel: id, snippet (title, customUrl, publishedAt) and
        statistics (viewCount, subscriberCount, videoCount as strings). Use it to confirm
        that the consent was given for the intended channel before updating videos, and
        as a cheap credential check. Costs 1 quota unit.
      params:
        mine:
          type: boolean
          in: query
          default: true
          description: "Keep true: return the channel of the authorized account."
        part:
          type: string
          in: query
          default: "snippet,statistics"
          description: "Comma-separated resource parts: id, snippet, statistics, status, contentDetails, brandingSettings."
      pagination: none

  composites:

    update_video:
      description: >
        Update a video of the authorized channel. Pass only what should change:
        visibility (privacy_status = private | unlisted | public), title, description,
        tags, category or flags. The composite reads the video, merges your changes into
        the current snippet and status and writes both parts back completely, so tags,
        language and all other fields you did not pass stay as they are. To swap one
        line of the description (for example a link) pass replace_line_prefix and
        replace_line_with: exactly one line must start with the prefix; if no line does
        but a line already equals the replacement, the description is left unchanged,
        so the call is safe to repeat. If nothing differs from the current state no
        write happens. Returns {id, changed, snippet, status}; `changed` lists the fields
        that were written (empty array = already in the requested state). The returned
        status reflects the write and is authoritative; a list_videos read in the first
        seconds afterwards may still show the previous privacyStatus, so verify with a
        delayed retry rather than an immediate read. Costs 1 quota unit for the read
        plus 50 units when something is written. Changing privacy_status to public
        publishes the video immediately.
      access: write
      params:
        id:
          type: string
          required: true
          description: "Video ID (11 characters). The video must belong to the authorized channel."
        privacy_status:
          type: string
          description: "private, unlisted or public."
        title:
          type: string
          description: "New title, max 100 characters, no angle brackets."
        description:
          type: string
          description: "New complete description, max 5000 bytes, no angle brackets. Do not combine with replace_line_prefix."
        replace_line_prefix:
          type: string
          description: "Replace the single description line that starts with this text. Requires replace_line_with."
        replace_line_with:
          type: string
          description: "The new content of that line."
        tags:
          type: array
          description: "New complete list of tags (replaces the current list)."
        category_id:
          type: string
          description: "Video category ID, for example 28 = Science & Technology."
        default_language:
          type: string
          description: "Language of title and description (BCP-47, for example de)."
        embeddable:
          type: boolean
          description: "Whether the video can be embedded on other sites."
        public_stats_viewable:
          type: boolean
          description: "Whether the extended statistics on the watch page are public."
        self_declared_made_for_kids:
          type: boolean
          description: "Creator's declaration that the video is made for kids."
        contains_synthetic_media:
          type: boolean
          description: "Disclosure that the video contains realistic altered or synthetic content."
        publish_at:
          type: string
          description: "Scheduled publication time (ISO 8601). Only valid while privacy_status is private."
      timeout: 30s
      depends_on: [list_videos, _update_video_raw]
      code: |
        const found = await api.list_videos({ id: params.id, part: "snippet,status" });
        const video = (found || []).filter(v => v.id === params.id)[0];
        if (!video) {
          throw new Error("video " + params.id + " not found or not visible to the authorized channel");
        }
        const cur = video.snippet || {};
        const curStatus = video.status || {};
        const changed = [];
        const pick = (name, value, current) => {
          if (value === undefined || value === null) { return current; }
          if (JSON.stringify(value) !== JSON.stringify(current)) { changed.push(name); }
          return value;
        };

        let description = cur.description || "";
        if (params.replace_line_prefix !== undefined && params.replace_line_prefix !== null) {
          if (params.description !== undefined && params.description !== null) {
            throw new Error("pass either description or replace_line_prefix, not both");
          }
          if (params.replace_line_with === undefined || params.replace_line_with === null) {
            throw new Error("replace_line_prefix requires replace_line_with");
          }
          const lines = description.split("\n");
          const hits = [];
          let already = false;
          for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
            const line = lines[i].trim();
            if (line === params.replace_line_with) { already = true; }
            else if (line.indexOf(params.replace_line_prefix) === 0) { hits.push(i); }
          }
          if (hits.length === 1) {
            lines[hits[0]] = params.replace_line_with;
            description = lines.join("\n");
            changed.push("description");
          } else if (!(hits.length === 0 && already)) {
            throw new Error("expected exactly one description line starting with the prefix, found " + hits.length);
          }
        } else {
          description = pick("description", params.description, description);
        }

        const snippet = {
          title: pick("title", params.title, cur.title),
          description: description,
          categoryId: pick("categoryId", params.category_id, cur.categoryId),
        };
        const tags = pick("tags", params.tags, cur.tags);
        if (tags !== undefined) { snippet.tags = tags; }
        const lang = pick("defaultLanguage", params.default_language, cur.defaultLanguage);
        if (lang !== undefined) { snippet.defaultLanguage = lang; }
        if (cur.defaultAudioLanguage !== undefined) { snippet.defaultAudioLanguage = cur.defaultAudioLanguage; }

        const status = { privacyStatus: pick("privacyStatus", params.privacy_status, curStatus.privacyStatus) };
        const flags = [
          ["embeddable", params.embeddable],
          ["publicStatsViewable", params.public_stats_viewable],
          ["selfDeclaredMadeForKids", params.self_declared_made_for_kids],
          ["containsSyntheticMedia", params.contains_synthetic_media],
          ["publishAt", params.publish_at],
        ];
        for (const f of flags) {
          const v = pick(f[0], f[1], curStatus[f[0]]);
          if (v !== undefined) { status[f[0]] = v; }
        }
        if (curStatus.license !== undefined) { status.license = curStatus.license; }

        if (changed.length === 0) {
          return { id: video.id, changed: changed, snippet: cur, status: curStatus };
        }
        const updated = await api._update_video_raw({ part: "snippet,status", id: video.id, snippet: snippet, status: status });
        return { id: video.id, changed: changed, snippet: (updated || {}).snippet, status: (updated || {}).status };

  hints:
    list_videos:
      empty_result: "an empty array means the ID is unknown or the video is private and belongs to another channel"
      statistics_strings: "statistics values are strings, convert before doing arithmetic"
    update_video:
      publishes: "privacy_status public takes effect immediately and is visible to everyone"
      quota: "1 unit when nothing changes, 51 units when something is written"
      line_swap: "replace_line_prefix must match exactly one description line"

  examples:
    - name: "Publish an unlisted video and swap its link line"
      description: "Make a video public and replace the description line that starts with a placeholder link"
      code: |
        const result = await api.update_video({
          id: "VIDEO_ID_11",
          privacy_status: "public",
          replace_line_prefix: "https://example.com/preview/",
          replace_line_with: "https://www.example.com/articles/launch/?utm_source=youtube",
        });
        return result.changed;
    - name: "Read visibility and view count"
      description: "Check whether a video is public and how often it was viewed"
      code: |
        const videos = await api.list_videos({ id: "VIDEO_ID_11", part: "status,statistics" });
        if (videos.length === 0) { return "not found or not visible"; }
        return { visibility: videos[0].status.privacyStatus, views: Number(videos[0].statistics.viewCount) };
